  <content>
  <section>
    <section class="check-understanding">
      <exercise data-content-id="fc849925-6fe7-4a85-8c37-8e6a82941051">
        <problem>
          <para>
      <para>
        For questions 1 - 5, use the the three exponential functions defined below:
      </para>
      <para>\(f(x)=100 \cdot 3^x\)</para>
        <para>\(g(x)=100 \cdot (3.5)^x\)</para>
        <para>\(h(x)=100 \cdot 4^x\)</para>
      <para> Which of these functions grows the least quickly?  </para>
      </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>f(x)</para>
          <para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)\). The value of \(f\) triples each time \(x\) increases by 1 because the growth factor (or the base) is 3. </para>
    </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </section>
